{'symbol': 'MAR', 'date': '2020-05-05 09:30:00', 'title': 'MARRIOTT INTERNATIONAL RAISES $920 MILLION IN CASH', 'text': 'MARRIOTT INTERNATIONAL RAISES $920 MILLION IN CASH THROUGH AMENDMENTS TO CO-BRAND CREDIT CARD AGREEMENTS WITH JPMORGAN CHASE & CO. AND AMERICAN EXPRESS.MARRIOTT - $570 MILLION FROM CHASE INCLUDES $500 MILLION OF PREPAYMENT OF CERTAIN FUTURE REVENUES.MARRIOTT - $570 MILLION FROM CHASE ALSO INCLUDES $70 MILLION FROM EARLY PAYMENT OF A PREVIOUSLY COMMITTED SIGNING BONUS UNDER CO-BRAND CREDIT CARD AGREEMENT.MARRIOTT - $350 MILLION FROM AMERICAN EXPRESS IS FOR PRE-PURCHASE OF MARRIOTT BONVOY POINTS AND OTHER CONSIDERATION.MARRIOTT - TERMINATED $1.5 BILLION 364-DAY REVOLVING CREDIT FACILITY COMMITMENT IT ANNOUNCED ON APRIL 14, 2020.'}